  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="742c7731-c35e-56b4-bee1-545c61cfe92c" activityNameId="22b5c36b-5826-57ec-b4c5-4337a7c24709" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ferromanganese, high-coal, 74.5% Mn, at regional storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ferromanganese, high-coal, 74.5% Mn, at regional storage
The module describes the consumption of ferromanganese in Europe in 1995. It is designed for the use of the metal as alloying element. This module does not consider secondary sources of manganese. Process data is taken mainly from a material flow analysis for the consumption of chromium in Germany. Results are used as a proxy for the European situation. This module may be used as proxy for the silicomanganese production;
UUID: e9d3e6de-15d4-379c-99d8-40155ad01fca
The module includes the reduction to high-carbon ferromanganese. No secondary production considered, since secondary manganese is recycled to the foundries and has to be inventoried in the respective module, i. e. when casting the final rawmaterial in the steel production.
Location: This module relates to the consumption in Europe, although the import mix for Germany is chosen.
Technology: The ore is processed in blast furnaces (20%), electric arc furnaces without flux (27%), electric arc furnaces with calcareous flux (53%).
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 3.4 million tonnes manganese contained in ferromanganese in 2001
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e9d3e6de-15d4-379c-99d8-40155ad01fca.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">RER</shortname>
        <comment>
